{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471938-escaping-gehenna-by-leaving-earth","id":1471938,"title":"Escaping Gehenna by leaving Earth","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-06T08:00:32-08:00","id":1471938,"title":"Escaping Gehenna by leaving Earth","content":"I remembered an old anime-film about vampires, Vampire Hunter D: Bloodlust. Basically, the major character are a noble vampire and his human lover that tries to reach an anciend star launch facility ( the story features a post apocalyptic future ) in order to leave Earth and reach a space station called the City of Night, a refuge for vampires.<br /> <br /> So I tought: several description of Gehenna talks about the arrival of a comet called Wormwood - or the Red Star - who explodes in a bright crimson light visible only through Auspex and spreads a fine red mystical powder that, according to Gehenna pag 54, &quot;travels quickly and penetrates anything and everything, from the deepest holes in Earth to the bottom of the ocean and from the tallest peaks to the interior of airplanes in flight&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b><i>But what if one or more vampires managed to reach space ,meanwhile?</i></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T11:15:25-08:00","id":1471942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471938-escaping-gehenna-by-leaving-earth#post1471938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remembered an old anime-film about vampires, Vampire Hunter D: Bloodlust. Basically, the major character are a noble vampire and his human lover that tries to reach an anciend star launch facility ( the story features a post apocalyptic future ) in order to leave Earth and reach a space station called the City of Night, a refuge for vampires.<br /> <br /> So I tought: several description of Gehenna talks about the arrival of a comet called Wormwood - or the Red Star - who explodes in a bright crimson light visible only through Auspex and spreads a fine red mystical powder that, according to Gehenna pag 54, &quot;travels quickly and penetrates anything and everything, from the deepest holes in Earth to the bottom of the ocean and from the tallest peaks to the interior of airplanes in flight&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b><i>But what if one or more vampires managed to reach space ,meanwhile?</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, it would take considerably more than half a dozen vampires to make anything feasbile - you'd need several reasonably large herds and even larger group of unwitting prey, for starters.<br /> <br /> Unless everybody is in the know because it's some crazy project like &quot;Carthage IN SPACE&quot; or somesuch from either Brujah idealists, anarchs or a mix of both. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T11:20:05-08:00","id":1471943,"title":"","content":"Unless we set this at a point in the future where there's sustainable human habitation in space? The vampire most likely starves, goes into torpor, and dies as nobody's at the controls to handle the exceedingly dangerous thing that is space travel (even just trying to maintain a stable orbit for long enough to Wordwood's effects to subside).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T12:17:32-08:00","id":1471947,"title":"","content":"An expert in Thaumaturgy can store a point of Vitae in an object small like a coin. If he prepares things in advance he can store more or less ten years worth of Vitae in a medium suitcase.<br /> <br /> That said, a vampire needs definetly less than a living human in order to survive space travel. Solved the Vitae problem, there's no need for water, food, sanitary services. Also vampire feel much less things like extreme acceleration, heat inferior than fire, levels of cold that would kill any living beings, things like compression and decompression and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T14:49:05-08:00","id":1471952,"title":"","content":"Are we seriously going to do the whole, &quot;Oh, well, the vampire has X Discipline/power/Merit whenever a new obstacle comes up?&quot; song and dance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T15:12:46-08:00","id":1471953,"title":"","content":"Why not. If a vampire that believed in Gehenna come up with a plan to escape the end and has enough time to prepare himself, he could arrange things well.<br /> <br /> But even if he relies on gallons of preserved blood, he's still better off than any human. Vampire are very resilient.<br /> <br /> Not to mention he can <i>pay</i> a vampire that possess the requisite power. Or they can share the spaceship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T15:44:28-08:00","id":1471957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471938-escaping-gehenna-by-leaving-earth?p=1471953#post1471953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's really unfun.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T16:33:57-08:00","id":1471965,"title":"","content":"Ok, but the true question is:<br /> <br /> assuming a vampire can succesfully do that, I see two possible outcomes:<br /> <br /> 1- The Creator cannot be tricked and the vampires get's the Wormwood anyway<br /> 2- The Creator cannot be tricked but since he extends his authority only on Earth, he leaves that lonely vampire eke out his miserable existence in the cold emptiness of deep space","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T19:36:19-08:00","id":1471969,"title":"","content":"I read the question as being, at heart, &quot;can a vampire come up with such a clever trick that they can escape the wrath of God?&quot;<br /> <br /> A hard one-size-fits-all answer to that doesn't exist; there's only the answer that suits the gaming group and the tone and theme of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T00:49:43-08:00","id":1471986,"title":"","content":"Is this feasible? Yes, it is. Is it likely to work? I don't think so.<br /> <br /> The preparation for such a project alone would mean this vampire can't do it in response to the Red Star approaching. The space launch of an unmanned probe still take years of preparation because of the extreme calculations involved and it has to wait for the right moment to launch. That goes before any other preparation the vampire will take to survive the trip. So such a scenario would probably involve a vampire that went to space for unrelated reasons.<br /> <br /> Lets assume then such a vampire exists. Then we have to decide how much time this journey will take. Space travel must be planned to the last detail beforehand. Is this a time in orbit and then come down? Is this a two-way mission to somewhere like the Apollo landings? Is it a permanent leave for another region of the universe entirely? The bigger the time the vampire expects to be in space, the greater the need for supplies, and any journey to another celestial body besides the Moon is going to take years, so journeying farther increases the difficulties and credibility of this voyage extremely quickly.<br /> <br /> Once the vampire is out of Earth... still, as you say, it depends a lot on how the ST takes it. There is no reachable conclusion of how any Gehenna scenario whatsoever would unfold, it does what the ST wants it to do. Instead, it is far more relevant and interesting to think about how things would unfold once this vampire reaches destination. So now I must ask: what is this destination? Earth under mortal control some years in the future, with this character as the last vampire? A space colony? What would be the point?<br /> <br /> Without a set goal the likely destiny of this vampire is destruction after untold eons in torpor for lack of blood, because an entire spaceship worth of Vitae through that ritual won't cover a fraction of the time for our fastest vessel to reach even the next star, and then the landing will be quite shocking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T02:26:06-08:00","id":1471988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I read the question as being, at heart, &quot;can a vampire come up with such a clever trick that they can escape the wrath of God?&quot; </div> </div> </div>No, it's completely different.<br /> <br /> <b>Let's just assume for a moment that space travel is feasible, one way or another.</b><br /> <br /> The point is: although the WoD Creator certainly CAN extend his Wormwood to all the universe, is he willing to do it?<br /> Because according to the WoD mythology, that Creator only created ( or &quot;rearranged / terraformed / shaped&quot; ) Earth to be the home of his humans.<br /> So, if a vampire manages to exist somewhere else, he's no longer preying upon the Creator's &quot;garden for human beings&quot;.<br /> <br /> The point is: does the Creator extends his sovereignity even on lifeless rocks that he didn't shape for life or unlife?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T03:06:30-08:00","id":1471991,"title":"","content":"There's no way to know, because the game never talks about it, because the game never considered this scenario worth even a few sentences of consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T11:21:52-08:00","id":1472010,"title":"","content":"What is Gehenna exactly? If it is anything in line with what was shown in the Time of Judgement books, the withering is going to get you no matter if you are on planet or outside of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T12:25:09-08:00","id":1472015,"title":"","content":"In the first scenario ( Wormwood ) the spiritual crimson gas engulf all the Earth, but only Earth.<br /> <br /> The point of my idea is that a vampire who managed to build a station on Mars, or a self sufficent ship, is eking a life outside the world that the Creator ( demiurge? ) modeled for humans.<br /> The vampire could protest to the Creator &quot;I'm not in your garden anymore, you haven't the right ( moral right ) to pursue me here&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T13:03:26-08:00","id":1472018,"title":"","content":"An indifferent Creator doesn't give a shit, because the harshness of life off of Earth is such that even a being as hardy as a vampire is still going to die soon enough.<br /> <br /> As vengeful Creator flings a car-engine sized chunk of rock at the vampire for being a little shit and the vampire dies immediately.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T13:26:15-08:00","id":1472020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471938-escaping-gehenna-by-leaving-earth?p=1472015#post1472015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the first scenario ( Wormwood ) the spiritual crimson gas engulf all the Earth, but only Earth.<br /> <br /> The point of my idea is that a vampire who managed to build a station on Mars, or a self sufficent ship, is eking a life outside the world that the Creator ( demiurge? ) modeled for humans.<br /> The vampire could protest to the Creator &quot;I'm not in your garden anymore, you haven't the right ( moral right ) to pursue me here&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to most WoD books the creator has left earth a long time ago. If you go by Mage's cosmology reaching Mars won't do you much good anyway. Also, are you sure the &quot;garden&quot; refers only to earth and not to all of the creation (again, going by Mage's cosmology what's on Mars kind of depends on who's on earth anyway...)?<br /> <br /> Gehenna was dealt with as an open concept. You (as the ST) decide what happens and who's responsible. If you want this little &quot;cheat&quot; to work... sure, go for it (disregarding the fact Gehenna supposedly happened at the start of the 3rd millenium) but it's just your decision, personally mixing sci-fi and vampire is not my cup of tea (a bit of Technocracy conflict is though...) but if you want to tell such a story... why not?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T14:15:38-08:00","id":1472021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471938-escaping-gehenna-by-leaving-earth?p=1471991#post1471991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no way to know, because the game never talks about it, because the game never considered this scenario worth even a few sentences of consideration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's better to elaborate from here. <b>This</b> is the point.<br /> <br /> As written, WoD is <b><i>extremely</i></b> human-centric. The setting doesn't just plays itself out of a human perspective, it plays on the notion that the human perspective and human existence is <b>objectively</b> the only one that matters, period. That does have variations with the lines, but even with Werewolf we have a few pieces that don't fit outside a human perspective, and we're not talking Werewolf anyway.<br /> <br /> So all the information we have is about Earth, and all of it plays humanity at the center of everything. We don't even know if there actually <b>is</b> a space to begin with, or if it is just a complex mirage over the hard limit of reality. Maybe the God of WoD isn't really that powerful and can't reach beyond the Moon, or Mars, and other, unknown entities govern other regions. Maybe this God created the entire universe and keeps several, even infinite worlds out there, and an escaping vampire would face the consequences of messing with grander plans, whatever those are. Maybe there's no universe outside the reach of God, and this vampire physically can't escape in a space vessel.<br /> <br /> We are in this level of darkness about the setting as a whole here. Many books hinted that even our most basic assumptions about the universe may be wrong (or outright stated they're wrong), but none gave us enough information to picture anything beyond. The best shot we have are some books about the Umbra, and they're not only hard to read and make sense of, but once you do they still don't give you nearly adequate answers to what lies beyond. Instead it just reinforces how freaking important is this lone round stone floating in the vastness of the cosmos, to the point that it is basically surrounded by the limits of meaningful reality.<br /> <br /> No meaningful conclusion can be drawn for the God of the WoD except that it probably exists. Not its power, its numbers, its actual intentions or anything. Demon, more than any line, does a great job at highlighting how utterly ignorant even its greatest servants are about God, your bit of Cosmic Horror right there. The world was created by something clearly with intentions and capable of arbitrary intervention, but ultimately unknowable, amoral, and ultimately this may be all just a big, sick joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T16:05:52-08:00","id":1472029,"title":"","content":"Well, if it's the God that laughs at Caine at the end of Gehenna, it does not promise well indeed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}